          <Pad Id="OwxVPvm46RRDVgEJkuoW2M" Bounds="-593,156,540,1100" ShowValueBox="true" isIOBox="true" Value="03 - In or out.&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;Move the mouse across the shape: inside, the fill appears and CONTAINS flips. A yes/no&#xD;&#xA;question about space, answered every frame. You have built this a hundred times as a&#xD;&#xA;hit test - GIS calls it a SPATIAL PREDICATE, and gives it a definition sharp enough to&#xD;&#xA;disagree with your eyes.&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;The notch is the lesson: the cursor can be nearly surrounded and still OUTSIDE. Near is&#xD;&#xA;a feeling; inside is a fact. The exact boundary counts as outside too - Covers is the&#xD;&#xA;predicate that includes it.&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;Contains (A, B) and Within (A, B) are the same question named from either end, polygon&#xD;&#xA;first or point first, so a patch reads left to right whichever way its data flows.&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;PLAY: reshape the polygon - it is one spread of vertices, feeding NTS and the drawing&#xD;&#xA;alike. Wire CONTAINS somewhere else: a radius, a sound. More predicates (Intersects&#xD;&#xA;ships; Touches, Overlaps, Crosses) arrive as chapters need them.&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;This patch uses ONE package, VL.NetTopologySuite - the geometry act's exemption: a&#xD;&#xA;course with a hole in its opening act is worse than a node appearing in two places.&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;NEXT - three directions, no order:&#xD;&#xA;  Tutorial 04   how far, exactly - distance as a drawable line&#xD;&#xA;  Tutorial 02   where these shapes came from&#xD;&#xA;  Tutorial 06   the earth, when you are ready for it">
            <p:TypeAnnotation LastCategoryFullName="Primitive" LastDependency="VL.CoreLib.vl">
              <Choice Kind="TypeFlag" Name="String" />
            </p:TypeAnnotation>
            <p:ValueBoxSettings>
              <p:fontsize p:Type="Int32">11</p:fontsize>
              <p:stringtype p:Assembly="VL.Core" p:Type="VL.Core.StringType">Comment</p:stringtype>
            </p:ValueBoxSettings>
          </Pad>
